      "text": "To find \\( z \\) such that the projection of the vector \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix}\\) onto the vector \\(\\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\) is \\(\\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we start by recalling the formula for the projection of vector \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) onto vector \\(\\mathbf{b}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{a} = \\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}}{\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{b}\n\\]\n\nHere, \\(\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\). First, we calculate the dot product \\(\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 0 \\cdot (-3) + 3 \\cdot 5 + z \\cdot (-1) = 15 - z\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the dot product \\(\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = (-3)^2 + 5^2 + (-1)^2 = 9 + 25 + 1 = 35\n\\]\n\nThus, the projection of \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) onto \\(\\mathbf{b}\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{a} = \\frac{15 - z}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nWe are given that this projection is equal to \\(\\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\). Therefore, we can set up the equation:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nBy comparing the components, we see that the coefficients and the vectors match, so we can equate the scalar coefficients:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} = \\frac{12}{15}\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the right-hand side:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} = \\frac{4}{5}\n\\]\n\nCross-multiplying to solve for \\(z\\):\n\n\\[\n5(15 - z) = 4 \\cdot 35\n\\]\n\n\\[\n75 - 5z = 140\n\\]\n\nRearranging terms to isolate \\(z\\):\n\n\\[\n-5z = 140 - 75\n\\]\n\n\\[\n-5z = 65\n\\]\n\n\\[\nz = -\\frac{65}{5} = -13\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(z\\) is \\(\\boxed{-13}\\).",
