      "text": "The projection of a vector $\\mathbf{v}$ onto a vector $\\mathbf{u}$ is given by:\n\\[\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{u}} \\mathbf{v} = \\frac{\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{v}}{\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{u}} \\mathbf{u}.\\]\nIn this case, $\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}.$\nThe dot product $\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{v}$ is:\n\\[\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{v} = (-3)(0) + (5)(3) + (-1)(z) = 15 - z.\\]\nThe dot product $\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{u}$ is:\n\\[\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{u} = (-3)^2 + (5)^2 + (-1)^2 = 9 + 25 + 1 = 35.\\]\nTherefore, the projection is:\n\\[\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{u}} \\mathbf{v} = \\frac{15 - z}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}.\\]\nEquating the two expressions for the projection, we have:\n\\[\\frac{15 - z}{35} = \\frac{12}{35}.\\]\nSolving for $z,$ we find:\n\\[15 - z = 12 \\implies z = 3.\\]\nTherefore, $z = \\boxed{3}.$The answer is: 3",
